**Do you want to request a *feature* or report a *bug*?**
*feature*

I have an attribute like so:

```js
{
  productCategories: {
    title: 'Kayak',
    value: 'kayak',
    level: 1,
  } 
}
```

Currently, I have a `refinementList` widget, with the `attributeName` set to `productCategories.title`.

Works, but isn't quite what I want. I *want* to set the `attributeName` to simply `productCategories`, and the be able to use all of those properties to render (and filter) the template.

Here's my (non-working) attempt for configuring a `refinementList` widget:

```js
{
      attributeName: 'productCategories',
      templates: {
        item: (data) => {
          const template = Hogan.compile(defaultTemplates.item);

          if (data.level > 1) {
            return null;
          }
        
          return template.render(data);
        }
      },

      transformData: {
        item: (data) => {
          return Object.assign(data, {
            label: data.value.title,
            value: data.value.slug,
          });
        }
      }
}
```

↑ I'm attempting to set the `attributeName` to `productCategories`, hoping that that would pass the whole object as `data.value` to `transformData.item`. I'm also attempting to filter out items based on some other data in that object in in `templates.item`.

It seems like I need another method/option to prep the data?

Related: https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/issues/739
